  "description": "<p>It appears that the inheritance algorithm is not working correctly with acl:default  when the authorization has an acl:default predicate that references a child resource of the acls owner.</p>\n\n<p>To illustrate: </p>\n\n<p>Create the following resources:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>curl -X PUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/box -i\r\ncurl -X PUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/box/cookies -i\r\ncurl -X PUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/box/cookies/cookie -i\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>PUT the following acl to  <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl</a></p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>@prefix acl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .\r\n&lt;#authorization1&gt; a acl:Authorization;\r\n acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/box/cookies&gt;;\r\n acl:default &lt;/rest/box/cookies&gt;;\r\n acl:mode acl:Read;\r\n acl:agent \"testuser\".\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Using the following command:</p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>curl -X PUT -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/box/fcr:acl -H \"Content-Type: text/turtle\" -d \"@acl.ttl\"\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Then:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>\r\n# GET box produces 403 as expected\r\ncurl -u testuser:testpass http://localhost:8080/rest/box -i\r\n\r\n# GET cookies produces 200 as expected\r\ncurl -u testuser:testpass http://localhost:8080/rest/box/cookies -i\r\n\r\n# GET cookie produces 403 when it should return a 200 \r\ncurl -u testuser:testpass http://localhost:8080/rest/box/cookies/cookie -i </pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>",
